  "caption": "Quinn ate a giant burrito, went straight to run club, and got a stabbing pain under the ribs by minute four.\n\nA side stitch is very common. The leading idea is that the lining inside the tummy wall gets irritated, and a full gut plus bouncing adds friction. It often eases as fitness builds.\n\nWhat often helps: big meals two to four hours before, small sips in the last hour, water rather than sugary drinks, a gradual warm-up and running tall. Mid-run, slow belly breaths, pressing the spot, leaning away or walking can help it pass.\n\nBelly or chest pain at rest, fever, chest pressure, or pain spreading to the shoulder or jaw needs prompt medical care.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
